  "title": "15 January 1970: John Lennon's Bag One exhibition opens in London",
  "date": "1970-01-15",
  "content": "<div class=\"ast-post-format- single-layout-1\"><div class=\"entry-content clear\" itemprop=\"text\"><p>An exhibition of <a href=\"/people/john-lennon/\">John Lennon</a>’s erotic lithographs opened on 15 January 1970 at the London Arts Gallery at 22 New Bond Street, London W1. <span id=\"more-21420\"></span></p><p>The lithographs, known collectively as Bag One, had been drawn by Lennon in 1969, and chronicled his wedding ceremony and honeymoon with <a href=\"/people/yoko-ono/\">Yoko Ono</a>, and one of their bed-ins for world peace.</p><p>The Bag One Portfolio was published as a limited edition of 300, and contained 14 artworks. Each lithograph was signed by Lennon. The portfolio went on sale for £550, with individual prints priced at £40 each.</p><p>The exhibition lasted two weeks, but on the second day the gallery was raided and police officers confiscated eight of the 14 originals on the grounds of indecency.</p><div data-carousel-extra=\"{&quot;blog_id&quot;:1,&quot;permalink&quot;:&quot;https://www.beatlesbible.com/1970/01/15/john-lennon-bag-one-exhibition-opens-london/&quot;}\" id=\"gallery-1\" class=\"gallery galleryid-21420 gallery-columns-3 gallery-size-thumbnail\"><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon portrait\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1970/01/15/john-lennon-bag-one-exhibition-opens-london/john-lennon-bag-one_01/\"><img decoding=\"sync\" width=\"146\" height=\"200\" src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-bag-one_01-146x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"John Lennon: Bag One (1969)\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-21421\" srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-bag-one_01-146x200.jpg 146w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-bag-one_01-423x580.jpg 423w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-bag-one_01.jpg 700w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 146px) 100vw, 146px\" data-attachment-id=\"21421\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1970/01/15/john-lennon-bag-one-exhibition-opens-london/john-lennon-bag-one_01/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-bag-one_01.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"700,960\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"John Lennon: Bag One (1969)\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"<p>Bag One</p>\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-bag-one_01-700x960.jpg\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></a></div><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text gallery-caption\" id=\"gallery-1-21421\">\nBag One</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"gallery-item\"><div class=\"gallery-icon portrait\">\n<a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1970/01/15/john-lennon-bag-one-exhibition-opens-london/john-lennon-bag-one_02_poets-page/\"><img decoding=\"sync\" width=\"150\" height=\"200\" src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-bag-one_02_poets-page-150x200.jpg\" class=\"attachment-thumbnail size-thumbnail\" alt=\"John Lennon: Bag One (1969) - Poet's Page\" aria-describedby=\"gallery-1-21422\" srcset=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-bag-one_02_poets-page-150x200.jpg 150w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-bag-one_02_poets-page-434x580.jpg 434w, https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-bag-one_02_poets-page.jpg 700w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 150px) 100vw, 150px\" data-attachment-id=\"21422\" data-permalink=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1970/01/15/john-lennon-bag-one-exhibition-opens-london/john-lennon-bag-one_02_poets-page/\" data-orig-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-bag-one_02_poets-page.jpg\" data-orig-size=\"700,936\" data-comments-opened=\"1\" data-image-title=\"John Lennon: Bag One (1969) – Poet&amp;#8217;s Page\" data-image-description=\"\" data-image-caption=\"<p>Poet&amp;#8217;s Page</p>\" data-large-file=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/wp/media/john-lennon-bag-one_02_poets-page.jpg\" fetchpriority=\"high\"></a></div><figcaption class=\"wp-caption-text g