lub-liverpool-115/\">The Beatles live: Cavern Club, Liverpool (lunchtime)</a></li><li>1961: <a href=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/1961/01/15/live-casbah-coffee-club-liverpool-3/\">The Beatles live: Casbah Coffee Club, Liverpool</a></li></ul><p>Want more? Visit the <a title=\"Day after day: the Beatles' history\" href=\"/history/\">Beatles history section</a>.</p></div><div class=\"gm-map\" style=\"position: relative;height: 390px; width: 100%;\"><iframe data-lazyloaded=\"1\" src=\"about:blank\" name=\"gm-map-1\" allowfullscreen=\"\" data-src=\"https://www.beatlesbible.com/?geo_mashup_content=render-map&amp;map_data_key=3be909d52fe9f05550204bfa378504e8&amp;height=390&amp;width=100%&amp;add_overview_control=false&amp;zoom=16&amp;enable_street_view=false&amp;map_type=G_HYBRID_MAP&amp;name=gm-map-1&amp;object_id=21420&amp;map_content=single\" style=\"position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border: none; overflow: hidden;\" title=\"Geo Mashup Map\"></iframe></div>",
  "textContent": "An exhibition of John Lennon’s erotic lithographs opened on 15 January 1970 at the London Arts Gallery at 22 New Bond Street, London W1. The lithographs, known collectively as Bag One, had been drawn by Lennon in 1969, and chronicled his wedding ceremony and honeymoon with Yoko Ono, and one of their bed-ins for world peace.The Bag One Portfolio was published as a limited edition of 300, and contained 14 artworks. Each lithograph was signed by Lennon. The portfolio went on sale for £550, with individual prints priced at £40 each.The exhibition lasted two weeks, but on the second day the gallery was raided and police officers confiscated eight of the 14 originals on the grounds of indecency.\n\nBag One\n\nPoet’s Page\n\nThe Honeymoon\n\nI Do\n\nExchange of Rings\n\nBed In For Peace\n\nJohn and Yoko\n\nErotic 1\n\nErotic 2\n\nErotic 3\n\nErotic 4\n\nErotic 5\n\nErotic 6\n\nErotic 7\n\nErotic 8Page last updated: 16 February 2026Also on this day...2025: Ringo Starr live: Ryman Auditorium, Nashville1979: John Lennon buys Steinway upright piano1979: Recording: Daytime Nighttime Suffering by Wings1976: Recording: Time To Hide, Wino Junko by Wings1975: Paul and Linda McCartney visit John Lennon1973: Mixing: Power Cut by Wings1969: George Harrison rejoins The Beatles1967: McCartney and Harrison watch Donovan in London1965: Live: Another Beatles Christmas Show1964: The Beatles live: Cinéma Cyrano, Versailles1962: The Beatles live: Cavern Club, Liverpool (lunchtime)1961: The Beatles live: Casbah Coffee Club, LiverpoolWant more? Visit the Beatles history section.",
